# Shared-checkout housekeeping

**Invariant:** `¬attribute(path, this_session ∨ this_dispatch) ⇒ ¬delete(path) ∧ ¬revert(path)`.
On Lane-A sole shared `master`, untracked / dirty / “noise” is often **parallel WIP** — not disposable.
Lane-B cursor-sdk worktrees carry their own dirty state on `cursor-sdk/lane-{thread}` —
do not `git clean` or delete paths there without session attribution either.

Doctrine: Use the `git-posture` skill (sole-checkout corollary). Friction class: a:25030.

## Forbidden

| Action | Why |
|---|---|
| `rm` / `rm -rf` / `git clean` of untracked paths because they are `??`, same-mtime as your job, or absent from `files_expected` | Those signals ≠ authorship |
| Treating implement `status=partial` / capture “unattributed paths” as license to delete | Capture grades dirty shared trees; it does not own them |
| “Safe housekeeping” without session/author proof or operator confirm | Overconfidence; irreversible |

## Permitted

| Action | When |
|---|---|
| Leave + flag (bus/scoreboard tangential) | Default |
| Ask operator before delete | Ambiguous ownership |
| Delete / revert | Proven this session/dispatch authored it, **or** operator explicitly directs |

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| “Untracked + Stage-B mtime ⇒ worker noise ⇒ `rm -rf cursor-plugins/`” | Flag as parallel-WIP candidate; leave alone |
| “Not in my `files_expected` ⇒ safe to clean” | `¬in(files_expected)` ≠ `owned_by(me)` |
| Infer disposable from `git status` alone | Attribute via session/dispatch evidence, then act |

**Confidence rule:** cannot trace origin ⇒ **not** safe to delete.
